From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Douglas Panhota <douglaspands@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: rockchip: keep the fractional divider input at 600 MHz
 or less

On the R36S V5 (PX30/RK3326) the sound plays low and slow. With the I2S1
master clock reported at 12.288 MHz (48 kHz x 256), 10 s of 48 kHz frames
written straight to hw:0,0 took 10.44 s (S16_LE) and 10.62 s (S32_LE), and
in games the rate wandered between 45 700 and 47 200 frames/s; a 440 Hz
sine came out near 411 Hz.

The clock tree shows clk_i2s1_frac fed by clk_i2s1_src at 1200 MHz (the
whole GPLL). The Rockchip vendor kernel caps the input of every PX30
fractional divider (I2S, PDM, UART) at 600 MHz (PX30_FRAC_MAX_PRATE in its
clk-px30.c, enforced in rockchip_fractional_approximation()), and the
factory system runs clk_i2s1_src at GPLL / 2 (CLKSEL_CON30 0x0401).

Apply the same 600 MHz cap here: when the divider input is above it, ask
the clock above for its parent rate divided down to the cap, so the
fractional divider works from 600 MHz.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk.c b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk.c
index 2d30b1e..2e69216 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk.c
@@ -174,6 +174,14 @@ static int rockchip_clk_frac_notifier_cb(struct notifier_block *nb,
 	return notifier_from_errno(ret);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Highest input rate of a fractional divider. The Rockchip vendor kernel caps
+ * it at 600 MHz on the PX30 (PX30_FRAC_MAX_PRATE, on the I2S, PDM and UART
+ * dividers). Fed with the 1200 MHz GPLL, the PX30 I2S1 master clock came out
+ * 2% to 6% slow and unsteady (R36S V5: 10 s of 48 kHz frames took 10.44 s).
+ */
+#define ROCKCHIP_FRAC_MAX_PRATE		600000000
+
 /*
  * fractional divider must set that denominator is 20 times larger than
  * numerator to generate precise clock frequency.
@@ -187,10 +195,15 @@ static void rockchip_fractional_approximation(struct clk_hw *hw,
 	struct clk_hw *p_parent;
 
 	p_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(clk_hw_get_parent(hw));
-	if ((rate * 20 > p_rate) && (p_rate % rate != 0)) {
+	if (((rate * 20 > p_rate) && (p_rate % rate != 0)) ||
+	    p_rate > ROCKCHIP_FRAC_MAX_PRATE) {
 		p_parent = clk_hw_get_parent(clk_hw_get_parent(hw));
-		p_parent_rate = clk_hw_get_rate(p_parent);
+		p_parent_rate = p_parent ? clk_hw_get_rate(p_parent) : p_rate;
 		*parent_rate = p_parent_rate;
+		/* ask the divider above for an input within the limit (GPLL / 2) */
+		if (p_parent_rate > ROCKCHIP_FRAC_MAX_PRATE)
+			*parent_rate = p_parent_rate /
+				       DIV_ROUND_UP(p_parent_rate, ROCKCHIP_FRAC_MAX_PRATE);
 	}
 
 	fd->flags |= CLK_FRAC_DIVIDER_POWER_OF_TWO_PS;
